{
  "manufacturer": "INVT",
  "manufacturer_slug": "invt",
  "model": "Goodrive10 (GD10) mini VFD",
  "model_slug": "goodrive10-gd10",
  "short_model": "GD10",
  "aliases": [
    "GD10",
    "Goodrive10",
    "GD10 mini VFD"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "INVT Goodrive10 mini drives using the built-in RS-485 Modbus RTU port, per the GD10 VFD manual V2.9 (chapter 7).",
  "summary": "INVT's small V/F drive for fans, pumps and light machinery. The built-in RS-485 port speaks Modbus RTU. A reduced command block (2000H-2003H, 200AH, 200BH, 200DH) takes run commands and setpoints, status and fault words sit at 2100H-2103H, monitors at 3000H onwards, and each function parameter has its own hex address. This map covers those plus the run-source, P14 serial and fault parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are printed in hex and go on the wire unchanged. Parameter P00.00 sits at 0000H and the manual's example frames carry the address bytes directly (writing P00.01 is sent as 01 06 00 01 00 03, and the read example asks for state word 2100H)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Goodrive10 Series Mini VFD Operation Manual",
    "doc_number": "V2.9",
    "revision_date": "2025-04",
    "url": "https://www.invt.com/uploads/file1/20250902/GD10%20VFD%20Manual_V2.9.pdf",
    "pages": "P00 group, P07.27 fault list, pp. 71-73 (P14 group), pp. 94-99 (7.3.4 addresses, examples)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Every register is a single 16-bit word; there are no 32-bit values in this map.",
    "Any function parameter can be read or written at (group << 8) | index; only the parameters an integrator needs most are listed here.",
    "3016H (identification code) and 5000H (fault code) are printed without range or unit, so they are left out; 2102H and 2103H carry the same information.",
    "GD10 has a smaller command block than other Goodrive drives: only 2000H-2003H, 200AH, 200BH and 200DH are listed. 300EH, 300FH, 3011H and 3013H are reserved.",
    "200BH is printed as 'Virtual input terminal command, range 0x00-0x0F' (the same name as 200AH); the range matches the virtual output command of other Goodrive drives.",
    "2100H code 0002H is printed as 'Forward running' a second time; sister INVT manuals use it for reverse running.",
    "This manual has no P00.02 entry; P00.01 = 2 is enough to take run commands from Modbus.",
    "Fault codes are the ones listed for GD10 (no 1-3, 13-14, 19-20, 23, 26-35)."
  ],
